hadiths[211]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7864","Abd Allah ibn Amr رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that in Paradise there is a chamber whose outside is seen from its inside and whose inside is seen from its outside. Abu Musa al-Ashari رضي الله عنه asked for whom it is, and he replied that it is for whoever softens speech, feeds food, and stands praying for Allah at night while people sleep. > **""In Paradise there is a chamber whose outside is seen from its inside and whose inside is seen from its outside. It is for whoever softens speech, feeds food, and stands for Allah at night while people sleep.""**"
"7865","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه said that when he saw the Prophet ﷺ his soul felt good and his eye felt cool, so he asked to be told about everything, and the Prophet ﷺ told him everything is created from water. He then asked for a deed that would admit him to Paradise, and the Prophet ﷺ commanded spreading peace, feeding food, joining kinship, and praying at night while people sleep, then entering Paradise in peace. > **""Everything is created from water. Spread peace, feed food, join kinship, pray at night while people sleep, then enter Paradise in peace.""**"
"7866","Hamzah ibn Suhayb reported that Suhayb was called Abu Yahya, claimed Arab lineage, and fed much food. Umar ibn al-Khattab رضي الله عنه asked why he used that kunya without a son, claimed Arab origin, and fed abundantly as extravagance. Suhayb replied that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had given him that kunya, that he was from al-Namir ibn Qasit of Mosul captured as a young boy yet remembering his family, and that he fed because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say to feed food and return greeting. > **""Feed food and return greeting.""**"
"7867","Anas رضي الله عنه reported that a man asked the Prophet ﷺ to teach him a deed that would admit him to Paradise, and he commanded feeding food, spreading peace, speaking good words, and praying at night while people sleep, so as to enter Paradise in peace. > **""Feed food, spread peace, speak good words, and pray at night while people sleep; you shall enter Paradise in peace.""**"
"7868","Habib ibn Abi Thabit said a woman of al-Husayn's household prepared food on one of his lands, he ate, the food was lifted, then his freed slave came and food was offered but he declined saying he had just eaten with Ubayd Allah ibn Abbas. Al-Husayn replied that the latter's father was the chief of Quraysh, and cited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressing Banu Abd al-Muttalib to feed food and sweeten speech. > **""O Banu Abd al-Muttalib, feed food and sweeten speech.""**"
"7869","Al-Hasan ibn Ali رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded feeding food and sweetening speech. > **""Feed food and sweeten speech.""**"
"7870","Jabir رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said feeding food enables Paradise, addressing Banu Abd al-Muttalib to feed food and sweeten speech. > **""Feeding food enables you to reach Paradise. O Banu Abd al-Muttalib, feed food and sweeten speech.""**"
"7871","Muhammad ibn Ziyad said Abd Allah ibn al-Harith used to pass by them saying the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded feeding food and spreading peace, by which Gardens are inherited. > **""Feed food and spread peace; you shall inherit the Gardens.""**"
"7872","Miqdam ibn Shurayh reported from his father from his grandfather that he asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for something that would obligate Paradise for him, and he replied that feeding food and spreading peace obligates Paradise, with another narration adding good speech. > **""Feeding food and spreading peace obligates Paradise.""** > **""And good speech.""**"
"7873","Imran ibn Husayn رضي الله عنه said the generous feeders who were also fed have gone, the remindful have gone, and only the delayers remain. Al-Hasan added that by Allah, were Imran alive today he would speak even more."
"7874","Abu al-Darda رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said whoever satisfies his brother's craving is forgiven. > **""Whoever satisfies his brother's craving is forgiven.""**"
"7875","Ismah reported that some Companions came to the Prophet ﷺ saying they passed markets, saw fruits, desired them, yet had no cash to buy, and asked whether there is reward in that. He asked whether reward is anything but that. > **""Is reward anything but that?""**"
"7876","Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn Talhah said he was with his uncle Isa ibn Talhah in the mosque when al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid entered and sent for him through Musa ibn Talhah to ask whether he had seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Al-Sa'ib affirmed he had seen him and had entered upon him with boys, finding him eating dates from a basket with some Companions, whereupon he scooped handfuls for them and wiped their heads."
"7877","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ invoked blessing in tharid and in suhur."
"7878","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said suhur is blessing, tharid is blessing, and congregation is blessing. > **""Suhur is blessing, tharid is blessing, and congregation is blessing.""**"
"7879","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ invoked blessing for three things: suhur, tharid, and the measure."
"7880","Anas رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to make tharid even if only with water. > **""Make tharid even if only with water.""**"
"7881","Jabir ibn Abdillah رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said when cooking meat to increase the broth or water, for it reaches further among neighbours. In al-Bazzar's wording, when cooking a pot increase its water or broth and look after neighbours. > **""When you cook meat, increase the broth or water, for it reaches further among neighbours.""** > **""When you cook a pot, increase its water or broth and look after your neighbours.""**"
"7882","Asma bint Abi Bakr رضي الله عنها used to cover tharid until its heat subsided, saying she heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say that is greater for blessing. > **""It is greater for blessing.""**"
"7883","Juwayriyah رضي الله عنها reported that the Prophet ﷺ disliked food being eaten until the burst of its steam had gone."
"7884","Khawlah bint Qays, wife of Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib, said the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon her, she prepared khazirah and offered it, he put his hand in, felt its heat, withdrew it, and said they do not bear heat or cold. He added that Allah gave him al-Kawthar, a river in Paradise, and no creature coming to it from her people is dearer to him, then continued the report. > **""O Khawlah, we do not bear heat or cold. O Khawlah, Allah has given me al-Kawthar, a river in Paradise, and no creature dearer to me shall come to it than those of your people.""**"
"7885","In another narration Khawlah said she brought him asidah in a vessel, and when he put his hand to it he said it burned, then said hiss, then said that when good befalls the son of Adam he says hass, and when cold befalls him he says hass. > **""It has burned. Hiss. When good befalls the son of Adam he says, Hass, and when cold befalls him he says, Hass.""**"
"7886","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ was brought a boiling dish, hastened his hand to it, then raised it and said Allah Almighty did not feed them fire. > **""Allah Almighty did not feed us fire.""**"
"7887","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to let food cool, for hot food has no blessing. > **""Let food cool, for hot food has no blessing.""**"
"7888","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ forbade blowing into food and drink."
"7889","Zayd ibn Thabit رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade blowing in prostration and in food."
"7890","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reported that the Prophet ﷺ would not blow into food or drink."
"7891","Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said not to sniff food as wild beasts sniff it. > **""Do not sniff food as wild beasts sniff it.""**"
"7892","Anas رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ never had a lunch or dinner of bread and meat brought together for him except amid a crowd."
"7893","Jabir رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the food most beloved to Allah is that over which most hands gather. > **""The food most beloved to Allah is that over which most hands gather.""**"
"7894","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to eat together and not separately, for the food of one suffices two and the food of two suffices four. > **""Eat together and do not separate, for the food of one suffices two and the food of two suffices four.""**"
"7895","Samurah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the food of one suffices two, the food of two suffices four, and the hand of Allah Almighty is over the congregation. > **""The food of one suffices two, the food of two suffices four, and the hand of Allah Almighty is over the congregation.""**"
"7896","Samurah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said whoever prepares food enough for two will find it suffices three, and whoever prepares food enough for four will find it suffices five. > **""Whoever prepares food enough for two will find it suffices three, and whoever prepares food enough for four will find it suffices five.""**"
"7897","Samurah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the food of one suffices two and the food of two suffices four. > **""The food of one suffices two, and the food of two suffices four.""**"
"7898","In another narration the Prophet ﷺ added that the food of four suffices eight. > **""And the food of four suffices eight.""**"
"7899","Abd Allah ibn Masud رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the food of one suffices two and the food of two suffices four. > **""The food of one suffices two, and the food of two suffices four.""**"
"7900","Ammar ibn Yasir رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not eat from a gift until ordering its owner to eat from it first, because of the sheep gifted to him at Khaybar."
"7901","Ibn A'bud said Ali ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنه asked him whether he knew the right of food, then taught him to say in the name of Allah and ask blessing in the provision, and taught him that its thanks after finishing is to say praise belongs to Allah who fed and gave drink."
"7902","A woman reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a leather bag of food which a Bedouin seized in three morsels, whereupon he remarked that had he said the name of Allah it would have sufficed all. He also said that if one forgets the name of Allah over food, let him say when he remembers that it is in the name of Allah at its beginning and end. > **""Had he said, In the name of Allah, it would have sufficed you.""** > **""If one of you forgets the name of Allah over his food, let him say when he remembers: In the name of Allah at its beginning and end.""**"
"7903","Anas رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said a man's food is placed and not lifted until he is forgiven. Asked how, he explained it is by saying the name of Allah when placed and praise to Allah when lifted. > **""A man's food is placed and not lifted until he is forgiven. He says, In the name of Allah, when it is placed, and, All praise belongs to Allah, when it is lifted.""**"
"7904","Ibn Masud رضي الله عنه reported that the devil of the Muslim meets the devil of the disbeliever, and the believer's devil appears pale, dusty, and emaciated. The other asks what ruined him, and he replies that he reaches nothing alongside his man, who mentions Allah's name when eating, drinking, and entering his house, while the other eats, drinks, and sleeps alongside his own man. Thus one is sleek and the other emaciated."
"7905","Abd Allah ibn Bishr رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ swore that Persia and Rome would be opened, the world poured forth, and bread and meat would become so abundant that Allah's name would not be mentioned over much of it. > **""By Him in whose hand is my soul, Persia and Rome shall be opened for you, the world shall be poured forth upon you, and bread and meat shall become so abundant that Allah's name shall not be mentioned over much of it.""**"
"7906","Salma, freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, reported that she prepared khazirah and brought it near, and he ate with some Companions leaving a little. A Bedouin passed, the Prophet ﷺ invited him, and he seized it all in his hand. The Prophet ﷺ told him to put it down, then to name Allah and eat from what is near so as to be satiated, whereupon he was satiated and some remained. > **""Put it down. Name Allah and eat from what is near; you shall be satiated.""**"
"7907","Hamzah ibn Amr al-Aslami رضي الله عنه said he ate food with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who told him to eat with his right, eat from what is near him, and mention Allah's name. > **""Eat with your right, eat from what is near you, and mention Allah's name.""**"
"7908","Abu Ayyub al-Ansari رضي الله عنه said they were with the Prophet ﷺ when food was brought near, and never saw food with more blessing at its start nor less at its end. Asked how, he explained they mentioned Allah's name when eating, then one who ate without naming sat afterwards and the devil ate with him. > **""Because we mentioned Allah's name when we ate, then one who ate without naming sat afterwards, so the devil ate with him.""**"
"7909","Jabir رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said whoever forgets to mention Allah's name at the start of his food should mention it at the end and recite that Allah is One. > **""Whoever forgets to mention Allah's name at the start of his food should mention Allah's name at its end and recite: Say, He is Allah, the One.""**"
"7910","Ibn Masud رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said whoever forgets to mention Allah's name at the start should say when he remembers that it is in Allah's name at its beginning and end, for he meets fresh food and withholds from the wicked one what it had taken. > **""Whoever forgets to mention Allah's name at the start of his food should say when he remembers: In Allah's name at its beginning and end, for he meets fresh food and withholds from the wicked one what it had taken.""**"
"7911","Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said when one's food is brought near while sandals are on his feet, let him remove them, for that is more restful for the feet. > **""When one's food is brought near while sandals are on his feet, let him remove his sandals, for that is more restful for the feet.""**"
"7912","In al-Tabarani's wording the Prophet ﷺ said when eating food to remove sandals, for that is more restful for the feet. > **""When you eat food, remove your sandals, for that is more restful for your feet.""**"
"7913","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reported from the Prophet ﷺ that ablution before and after food removes poverty and belongs to the practices of the Messengers. > **""Ablution before and after food removes poverty, and it belongs to the practices of the Messengers.""**"
"7914","A'ishah رضي الله عنها reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the angels continue praying for one of them so long as his table remains spread. > **""The angels continue praying for one of you so long as his table remains spread.""**"
"7915","Jabir رضي الله عنه said they were eating dates upon a shield when the Prophet ﷺ passed having come from relieving himself. They invited him, so he came forward and ate dates with them without touching water."
"7916","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that a man brought food to the Prophet ﷺ, who told him to put it on the low ground. > **""Put it on the low ground.""**"
"7917","Wathilah reported that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ conquered Khaybar a feast was prepared for him, and he ate reclining, oiled himself, and wore a shade when the sun struck him."
"7918","Abu al-Darda رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said not to eat reclining. > **""Do not eat reclining.""**"
"7919","Ibn Abi Ihab reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, or forbade them, to eat reclining. > **""Do not eat reclining.""**"
"7920","Abu Umamah رضي الله عنه reported from the Prophet ﷺ that eating in the market is meanness. > **""Eating in the market is meanness.""**"
"7921","Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade drinking standing, eating standing, the tied sacrificial animal, the dung-eating animal, and drinking from the mouth of the waterskin. > **""Do not drink standing, do not eat standing, and avoid the tied animal, the dung-eating animal, and drinking from the mouth of the waterskin.""**"
"7922","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما said the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered a garden of the Ansar eating fresh dates while walking with him, then turned and told him not to eat with two fingers since that is the devil's eating, but to eat with three fingers. > **""O Ibn Abbas, do not eat with two fingers, for that is the devil's eating; eat with three fingers.""**"
"7923","Amir ibn Rabi'ah رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ used to eat with three fingers and lick them when finished."
"7924","Anas رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man to eat or drink with his left."
"7925","A'ishah رضي الله عنها reported from the Prophet ﷺ that whoever eats with his left, the devil eats with him, and whoever drinks with his left, the devil drinks with him. > **""Whoever eats with his left, the devil eats with him, and whoever drinks with his left, the devil drinks with him.""**"
"7926","Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said when one eats let him not eat with his left, when he drinks let him not drink with his left, when he takes let him not take with his left, and when he gives let him not give with his left. > **""When one of you eats, let him not eat with his left; when he drinks, let him not drink with his left; when he takes, let him not take with his left; and when he gives, let him not give with his left.""**"
"7927","Hafsah, wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would lie on his right hand when retiring to bed, and his right was for his eating, drinking, ablution, clothing, taking, and giving, while he assigned his left to everything else."
"7928","Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Zayd reported from a woman among them that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon her while she ate with her left, as she was left-handed. He struck her hand so the morsel fell and told her not to eat with her left since Allah had given her a right, or that Allah had freed her right. She said her left then turned into a right and she never ate with it afterwards. > **""Do not eat with your left, for Allah has given you a right.""**"
"7929","Jarhad reported that he came to the Prophet ﷺ while food lay before him, and stretched his left hand to eat because his right was injured. The Prophet ﷺ told him to eat with the right, he pleaded injury, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ breathed upon it, after which he never complained of it until he died. > **""Eat with the right.""**"
"7930","Uqbah ibn Amir رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw Subay'ah al-Aslamiyyah eating with her left and asked what was wrong with her eating with her left, finding her insolent. She said there was a sore in her hand, and he replied even if it were the death of a cow. A plague then seized her and killed her. In another narration he asked where the death of a cow is. > **""What is wrong with her eating with her left? Even if it were the death of a cow.""**"
"7931","Umar ibn al-Khattab رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said none should eat with his left, for the devil eats and drinks with his left. > **""Let none of you eat with his left, for the devil eats with his left and drinks with his left.""**"
"7932","Umar ibn Abi Salamah رضي الله عنه reported that food was brought near to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who told his Companions to mention Allah's name and let each eat from what is before him. > **""Mention Allah's name, and let each eat from what is before him.""**"
"7933","Ja'far ibn Abdillah said al-Hakam al-Ghifari saw him as a boy eating from here and there and told him not to eat so, for so eats the devil. He added that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed his hand in the bowl his fingers would not pass the place of his palm."
"7934","A'ishah رضي الله عنها reported that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate food his hand would not go beyond what lay before his eyes, but when dates were brought his hand would roam."
"7935","Abd Allah ibn Busr رضي الله عنه said his father sent him to invite the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to food, so he came along, hurried ahead to inform his parents, and they welcomed the Prophet ﷺ and seated him on their striped cloth. His mother brought a bowl of flour kneaded with water and salt, and the Prophet ﷺ told them to take in Allah's name from its sides and leave its top, for blessing lies in it. They all ate, some remained, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed for forgiveness, mercy, blessing, and expanded provision for them. > **""Take in Allah's name from its sides and leave its top, for blessing lies in it.""** > **""O Allah, forgive them, have mercy on them, bless them, and expand their provision.""**"
"7936","Salma reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked taking from the top of food."
"7937","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما used to lick his fingers and cite the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying one does not know in which portion of his food the blessing lies. In the wording of Ahmad and al-Bazzar, when one eats let him not wipe his hand until he licks it, for the Prophet ﷺ said one does not know in which food the blessing lies. > **""You do not know in which portion of your food the blessing lies. When one of you eats, let him not wipe his hand until he licks it.""**"
"7938","Al-Irbad ibn Sariyah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said whoever licks the dish and licks his fingers, Allah will satiate him in this world and the Hereafter. > **""Whoever licks the dish and licks his fingers, Allah will satiate him in this world and the Hereafter.""**"
"7939","Jubayr ibn al-Muthanna reported from his father that Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan sent to Zayd ibn Thabit رضي الله عنه asking how he eats and drinks. He replied that he drinks until his breath is cut, then lifts the vessel from his mouth, and when he eats he licks his fingers, for he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say that when one eats he should lick his fingers since he does not know in which portion of his food the blessing lies. > **""When one of you eats, let him lick his fingers, for he does not know in which portion of his food the blessing lies.""**"
"7940","Abu al-Mada said Marwan ibn al-Hakam asked Zayd ibn Thabit رضي الله عنه how he eats. He cited Abu Sa'id al-Khudri رضي الله عنه reporting from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that when one tastes food he should not wipe his hand until he licks his fingers, since he does not know in which portion blessing is granted to him. > **""When one of you tastes food, let him not wipe his hand until he licks his fingers, for he does not know in which portion of it blessing is granted to him.""**"
"7941","Ka'b ibn Ujrah رضي الله عنه said he saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ eating with his three fingers, the thumb and the one next to it, licking the middle one, then the one next to it, then the thumb."
"7942","Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said when one eats he should lick his three fingers, for he does not know in which of them the blessing lies. > **""When one of you eats, let him lick his three fingers, for he does not know in which of them the blessing lies.""**"
"7943","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه said the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he ate food, would lick his fingers and say that licking the fingers is blessing. > **""Licking the fingers is blessing.""**"
"7944","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reported that the Prophet ﷺ commanded licking the dish."
"7945","A man of Banu Sulaym who had companionship reported that the Prophet ﷺ, when he finished his food, would say praise and thanks to Allah who fed, gave drink, satiated, and quenched, with praise undenied, unbidden farewell, and never dispensed with. > **""O Allah, to You belongs praise. You fed, gave drink, satiated, and quenched. To You belongs praise, undenied, unbidden farewell, and never dispensed with.""**"
"7946","Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman said he dined with Abu Burdah, who cited his father Abd Allah ibn Qays reporting that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said whoever eats until satiated and drinks until quenched, then says praise to Allah who fed and satiated him and gave him drink and quenched him, exits his sins as on the day his mother bore him. > **""All praise belongs to Allah who fed me and satiated me, gave me drink and quenched me.""**"
"7947","Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he finished his food, would say praise to Allah who fed and gave drink, sufficed and sheltered, bestowed and favored, and ask by His mercy for deliverance from the Fire. > **""All praise belongs to Allah who fed us and gave us drink. All praise belongs to Allah who sufficed us and sheltered us. All praise belongs to Allah who bestowed upon us and favored us. We ask You by Your mercy to shield us from the Fire.""**"
"7948","Al-Harith ibn al-Harith رضي الله عنه said he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the end of his food say praise to Allah who fed, gave drink, satiated, and quenched, with praise undenied, unbidden farewell, and never dispensed with, O our Lord. > **""O Allah, to You belongs praise. You fed, gave drink, satiated, and quenched. To You belongs praise, undenied, unbidden farewell, and never dispensed with, O our Lord.""**"
"7949","Sa'd ibn Mas'ud al-Thaqafi said Nuh was named a thankful servant only because when he ate and drank he praised Allah."
"7950","Al-Harith ibn Suwayd reported that Salman al-Farisi رضي الله عنه, when he finished his food, would say praise to Allah who sufficed the burden and expanded provision."
"7951","Abu Ayyub رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said how excellent are the pickers. Asked who they are, he explained they are those who pick in ablution and those who pick from food. Picking in ablution is rinsing the mouth, the nostrils, and between the fingers, while picking from food is removing it from between the teeth, for nothing is harder upon the two angels than seeing food between the teeth of their companion while he stands praying. > **""How excellent are the pickers: those who pick in ablution and those who pick from food.""**"
"7952","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما said the excess food remaining between the molars weakens the molars."
"7953","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said whoever eats any of this meat should wash his hand of its smell and grease so as not to harm the one beside him. > **""Whoever eats any of this meat should wash his hand of its smell and grease so as not to harm the one beside him.""**"
"7954","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reported that the Prophet ﷺ said whoever spends the night with the smell of rich grease on his hand and harm befalls him should blame only himself. > **""Whoever spends the night with the smell of rich grease on his hand, and harm befalls him, let him blame only himself.""**"
"7955","Abu Sa'id رضي الله عنه reported from the Prophet ﷺ that whoever spends the night with the smell of grease on his hand and white harm befalls him should blame only himself. > **""Whoever spends the night with the smell of grease on his hand and harm befalls him, let him blame only himself.""**"
"7956","Al-Hakam said they were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at a meal when a man asked the household servant for a napkin, who handed him his own garment, with which he wiped. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said not to wipe with the garment of one whom he does not clothe. > **""Do not wipe with the garment of one whom you do not clothe.""**"
"7957","Abu Bakrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man to wipe with the garment of one whom he does not clothe."
"7958","A'ishah رضي الله عنها reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to dissolve food with remembrance of Allah and prayer, and not to sleep upon it lest hearts harden. > **""Dissolve your food with remembrance of Allah and prayer, and do not sleep upon it lest your hearts harden.""**"
"7959","Abu Juhayfah رضي الله عنه said he ate tharidah with fatty meat, came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ belching, and was told to withhold his belching from them, for the most satiated people in this world shall be the longest hungry on the Day of Resurrection. Thereafter Abu Juhayfah never filled his stomach until he left the world; when he ate lunch he skipped dinner, and when he ate dinner he skipped lunch. > **""Withhold your belching from us, O Abu Juhayfah, for the most satiated people in this world shall be the longest hungry on the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"7960","Abd Allah ibn Amr رضي الله عنهما said a man belched before the Prophet ﷺ, who told him to shorten his belching, for the longest hungry on the Day of Resurrection shall be the most satiated in this world. > **""Shorten your belching, for the longest hungry on the Day of Resurrection shall be the most satiated in this world.""**"
"7961","Al-Lajlaj said he never filled his stomach with food since he embraced Islam with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, eating his sufficiency and drinking his sufficiency, meaning his sustenance."
"7962","Ja'dah reported that the Prophet ﷺ saw a man with a huge belly, poked it with his finger, and said had this been elsewhere it would have been better for him. In another narration, a man related a dream to him while huge-bellied, and he poked his belly saying had this been elsewhere it would have been better for him. > **""Had this been elsewhere it would have been better for you.""**"
"7963","Abu Basrah al-Ghifari رضي الله عنه said he came to the Prophet ﷺ when he migrated, just before embracing Islam, and the Prophet ﷺ milked for him a small ewe he used to milk for his family, which he drank. In the morning he embraced Islam, while the Prophet's household said they would spend the night hungry as before. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ milked a ewe for him, he drank and was satisfied, and affirmed he had never been satiated or quenched before that day. The Prophet ﷺ then said the disbeliever eats in seven intestines while the believer eats in one intestine. > **""The disbeliever eats in seven intestines, and the believer eats in one intestine.""**"
"7964","Jahjah al-Ghifari reported that he came with a group of his people seeking Islam and attended Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who told each man to take the hand of his companion. None remained in the mosque except the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Jahjah, a huge tall man, so the Prophet ﷺ took him home, milked a goat which he finished, then seven goats which he finished, then a pot dish which he finished. Umm Ayman said may Allah starve whoever starved the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that night, but he told her hush, for he ate his provision while their provision is upon Allah. The next night, after Islam, he was again hosted, drank one goat's milk, was satiated and full, and the Prophet ﷺ explained that he had eaten that night in a believer's intestine after eating before in a disbeliever's intestine. > **""Hush, O Umm Ayman. He ate his provision, and our provision is upon Allah.""** > **""He ate tonight in a believer's intestine after eating before in a disbeliever's intestine. The disbeliever eats in seven intestines and the believer eats in one intestine.""**"
"7965","Abd Allah ibn Amr رضي الله عنهما said seven men came to the Prophet ﷺ, each Companion took one man and the Prophet ﷺ took a man named Abu Ghazwan. He milked seven ewes for him and he drank all their milk. The Prophet ﷺ invited him to Islam, he embraced it, and the Prophet ﷺ wiped his chest. In the morning the Prophet ﷺ milked one ewe for him and he could not finish its milk. Asked what was wrong, he swore by the truth that he was satisfied, and the Prophet ﷺ replied that yesterday he had seven intestines while today he has only one. > **""Yesterday you had seven intestines, and today you have only one.""**"
"7966","Abu Sa'id رضي الله عنه reported from the Prophet ﷺ like the preceding report that the believer eats in one intestine and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines. > **""The believer eats in one intestine and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines.""**"
"7967","Samurah رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said the believer eats in one intestine and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines, with one narration replacing disbeliever with hypocrite. > **""The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines.""**"
"7968","Sukayn al-Damri reported that the Prophet ﷺ said the believer eats in one intestine and the disbeliever in seven intestines. > **""The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever in seven intestines.""**"
"7969","Maymunah bint al-Harith رضي الله عنها said people suffered drought one year, Bedouins came to Madinah, and the Prophet ﷺ would order each man to take another by the hand and host him for dinner. One night a Bedouin came while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had only a little food and some milk; the Bedouin ate it all and left nothing. He returned a night or two eating everything, so she prayed that Allah not bless him for eating the Prophet's food. Then he came another night and ate only a little, and after he had embraced Islam the Prophet ﷺ explained that the disbeliever eats in seven intestines while the believer eats in one intestine. > **""The disbeliever eats in seven intestines, and the believer eats in one intestine.""**"
"7970","Mujahid said he asked Abu Sa'id how little his food was, and he replied he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say the disbeliever eats in seven intestines and the believer eats in one intestine. > **""The disbeliever eats in seven intestines and the believer eats in one intestine.""**"
"7971","Anas رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the believer eats in one intestine and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines. > **""The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines.""**"
"7972","Abd Allah ibn Abi Qays al-Nasri said he saw Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr رضي الله عنهما standing upon his pulpit in Makkah, preaching that the believer eats in one intestine and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines, adding that thus he heard their Prophet ﷺ."
"7973","Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه said the Prophet ﷺ was brought a vessel or cup containing milk and honey, and he said two condiments in one vessel he would neither eat nor forbid. > **""Two condiments in one vessel: I neither eat it nor forbid it.""**"
"7974","Abu al-Darda رضي الله عنه reported from the Prophet ﷺ that they should measure their food so blessing is granted in it. > **""Measure your food; blessing shall be granted to you in it.""**"
"7975","Al-Hasan ibn Ali رضي الله عنهما entered the place of ablution and found a morsel or piece of bread in the channel of filth and urine. He removed the harm, washed it well, handed it to his servant, and told him to remind him of it after ablution. When he finished he asked for it, but the servant said he had eaten it. Al-Hasan freed him for Allah. Asked why, he cited Fatimah bint Rasulillah ﷺ reporting from her father ﷺ that whoever takes a morsel from the channel of filth, removes its harm, washes it well, then eats it, it shall not settle in his stomach until he is forgiven, so he would not employ a man of Paradise. > **""Whoever takes a morsel from the channel of filth, removes its harm, washes it well, then eats it, it shall not settle in his stomach until he is forgiven.""**"
"7976","Abu Sukaynah reported that the Prophet ﷺ said to honor bread, for Allah honored it, and whoever honors bread, Allah honors him. > **""Honor bread, for Allah honored it. Whoever honors bread, Allah honors him.""**"
"7977","Abd Allah ibn Umm Haram رضي الله عنه said he prayed both qiblahs with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and heard him say to honor bread, for Allah Almighty sent it down from the blessings of heaven and subjected to it the blessings of earth, and whoever pursues what falls from the table is forgiven. > **""Honor bread, for Allah Almighty sent it down from the blessings of heaven and subjected to it the blessings of earth. Whoever pursues what falls from the table is forgiven.""**"
"7978","Abu al-Darda رضi الله عنه reported from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that they should make their food in small portions so blessing is granted in it. Ibrahim said he heard a scholar interpret it as making loaves small, as Ibn al-Athir likewise transmitted. > **""Make your food in small portions; blessing shall be granted to you in it.""**"
"7979","Salim, freed slave of Zayd ibn Suhan, said he was with his master in the market when Salman al-Farisi رضي الله عنه passed having bought a wasq of food. Zayd asked whether he does that while being a Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Salman replied that when the soul secures its provision it grows calm, devotes itself to worship, and the whisperer despairs of it."
"7980","Ubadah ibn al-Samit رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said when they see a red pillar before the east in Ramadan they should store their year's food, for it is a year of hunger. > **""When you see a red pillar before the east in Ramadan, store your year's food, for it is a year of hunger.""**"
"7981","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said drought is not the absence of rain, but drought is that people are rained upon while the earth yields no growth. > **""Drought is not that there is no rain; drought is that people are rained upon while the earth yields no growth.""**"
"7982","Abd Allah ibn Amr رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to take condiment even if only with water. > **""Take condiment even if only with water.""**"
"7983","Buraydah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the chief of condiments in this world and the Hereafter is meat, the chief of drinks in this world and the Hereafter is water, and the chief of fragrances in this world and the Hereafter is contentment. > **""The chief of condiments in this world and the Hereafter is meat, the chief of drinks in this world and the Hereafter is water, and the chief of fragrances in this world and the Hereafter is contentment.""**"
"7984","Rashid ibn Abi Rashid said Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه had a servant who made sausages for him, cooked two kinds of dishes, baked white bread for him, and kneaded it with ghee."
"7985","Abd Allah ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما said the Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked seven parts of the sheep: the gallbladder, the urinary bladder, the pudendum, the male organ, the two testicles, the gland, and blood, while the most beloved part of the sheep to him was its front. He added that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought food, people kept feeding him meat, and he said the tastiest meat is the meat of the back. > **""The tastiest meat is the meat of the back.""**"
"7986","Nusaykah Umm Amr ibn Jullas said she was with A'ishah رضي الله عنها when the latter slaughtered a sheep. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered holding a small stick, threw it, went to the mosque and prayed two rak'ahs, then went to his bed and reclined. He asked whether there was lunch, so they brought a dish with barley bread, a morsel, a piece of tripe, and the foreleg. A'ishah took a piece of tripe and was biting it when she said they had slaughtered a sheep that day and kept only this. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied that rather all of it was kept except this. > **""Is there any lunch? No, rather all of it you kept except this.""**"
"7987","Abd Allah ibn Ja'far رضي الله عنهما said the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was gifted a sheep and loaves, and as he and the people ate, he heard him say to keep to the meat of the back, for it is among the tastiest. > **""Keep to the meat of the back, for it is among the tastiest.""**"
"7988","Abu Amr al-Shaybani said Abd Allah saw dirhams with a man and asked what he would do with them. He said he would buy a faraq of ghee. Abd Allah told him to give them to his wife to place under her mattress, then buy meat each day for a dirham."
"7989","Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها reported that the Prophet ﷺ said not to cut bread with a knife as the non-Arabs cut it, and when one wants to eat meat he should not cut it with a knife but take it in his hand and tear it with his mouth, for that is more wholesome and agreeable. > **""Do not cut bread with a knife as the non-Arabs cut it. When one of you wants to eat meat, let him not cut it with a knife; let him take it in his hand and tear it with his mouth, for that is more wholesome and agreeable.""**"
"7990","Jabir رضي الله عنه said Qays ibn Sa'd ibn Ubadah passed them in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when famine struck, and slaughtered seven camels for them. They descended to the seashore and found an enormous fish, stayed by it three days, carried its fat in skins and sacks, then traveled until they came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him. They said had they known they would reach him before it departed, they would have loved to have some of it with them."
"7991","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said when one is brought perfume he should take some of it, and when brought sweet he should take some of it. > **""When one of you is brought perfume, let him take some of it, and when he is brought sweet, let him take some of it.""**"
"7992","Abd Allah ibn Salam رضي الله عنه said when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to the mirbad he saw Uthman ibn Affan رضي الله عنه leading a camel carrying flour, ghee, and honey. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said nakh, so he knelt it. He called for a pot, placed ghee, honey, and flour in it, ordered a fire kindled beneath until it cooked, then said eat. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate from it and said this is something the people of Persia call khabis. > **""Eat. This is something the people of Persia call khabis.""**"
"7993","Hudhayfah رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said Jibril fed him harisah to strengthen his back for standing at night. > **""Jibril fed me harisah to strengthen my back for standing at night.""**"
"7994","Anas رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ said when a fly falls into the vessel of one of them he should immerse it, for in one wing is disease and in the other is cure. > **""When a fly falls into the vessel of one of you, let him immerse it, for in one of its wings is disease and in the other is cure.""**"
"7995","Al-Rubayyi' bint Mu'awwidh رضي الله عنها said the Messenger of Allah ﷺ liked cucumber."
"7996","Abd Allah ibn Ja'far رضي الله عنهما said he was shown cucumber in the right hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and fresh dates in his left, eating from one once and from the other once."
"7997","Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to eat fresh dates with his right and watermelon with his left, eating dates with watermelon, and it was the most beloved fruit to him."
"7998","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما said he saw the Prophet ﷺ eating grapes by plucking them off the cluster."
"7999","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما said Jibril عليه السلام came to the Prophet ﷺ and said his Lord greets him with peace and sent him with this cluster to eat. > **""Your Lord greets you with peace and sent me with this cluster for you to eat.""**"
"8000","Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه said Jibril عليه السلام came to the Prophet ﷺ and said his Lord greets him with peace and sent him with this cluster to eat, whereupon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took it. > **""Your Lord greets you with peace and sent me with this cluster for you to eat.""**"
"8001","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reported that the Prophet ﷺ, when brought fruit, would give it to the youngest child present."
"8002","Ibn Abbas رضi الله عنهما said the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when brought the first fruits of the season, would place them upon his eyes and say O Allah, as You fed us its first, feed us its last, then order it for the newborn of his household. In an addition, he would kiss it and place it upon his eyes. > **""O Allah, as You fed us its first, feed us its last.""**"
"8003","Anas رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to A'ishah رضي الله عنها that when fresh dates arrive she should give him glad tidings. > **""When fresh dates arrive, give me glad tidings.""**"
"8004","Ali ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to honor their aunt the date-palm, for it was created from the clay from which Adam was created, and no tree other than it is pollinated. > **""Honor your aunt the date-palm, for it was created from the clay from which Adam was created, and no tree other than it is pollinated.""**"
"8005","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to feed women giving birth fresh dates, and if there are no fresh dates then dry dates, for no tree is nobler to Allah than the tree beneath which Maryam bint Imran gave birth. > **""Feed your women giving birth fresh dates, and if there are no fresh dates then dry dates. No tree is nobler to Allah than the tree beneath which Maryam bint Imran gave birth.""**"
"8006","Anas رضي الله عنه reported that the Prophet ﷺ was brought a dish containing unripe and fresh dates, and he ate the fresh dates while leaving the defective-tailed ones."
"8007","Abd Allah ibn Amr رضي الله عنهما reported from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that Allah Almighty loves whoever loves dates. > **""Allah Almighty loves whoever loves dates.""**"
"8008","Abd Allah ibn al-Aswad said they were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the delegation of Sadus and gifted him dates, presenting them on a leather mat. He took a handful, and Anas asked what this was. They kept naming until they mentioned dates, saying this is al-Judhami, whereupon he prayed for blessing in al-Judhami and in the garden whence it came. > **""Allah bless al-Judhami and the garden whence this came.""**"
"8009","Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه reported that the delegation of Abd al-Qays came to the Prophet ﷺ, and while sitting with him he turned to them naming the dates they call such and such until he counted all the kinds of their dates. A man said may his father and mother be ransom, had he been born inside Hajar he would not be more knowledgeable at this hour, and bore witness that he is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied that their land had been raised for him since they sat with him, so he saw it from nearest to farthest, and their best dates are al-Barni, which removes disease with no disease in it. > **""A date you call such and such, and a date you call such. Your land was raised for me since you sat with me, and I saw it from nearest to farthest. Your best dates are al-Barni; it removes disease with no disease in it.""**"
"8010","Abu Sa'id al-Khudri رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said their best dates are al-Barni; it removes disease with no disease in it. > **""Your best dates are al-Barni; it removes disease with no disease in it.""**"
"8011","Al-Hirmas said a man of his tribe gifted dates to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who asked what dates these were. He said al-Judhami, whereupon he prayed for blessing in al-Judhami. > **""What dates are these? O Allah, bless al-Judhami.""**"
"8012","Abd Allah ibn Salam رضي الله عنه said he saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ take a piece of barley bread, then take a date and place it upon it, then say this is the condiment of this. > **""This is the condiment of this.""**"
"8013","Zayd ibn Thabit رضي الله عنه said the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to eat bread with dates and say this is the condiment of this. > **""This is the condiment of this.""**"
"8014","A'ishah رضي الله عنها reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, addressing her, that this is the condiment of this, meaning dates and bread. > **""O A'ishah, this is the condiment of this.""**"
"8015","Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said whoever eats seven Ajwah dates between the two lava plains of Madinah on an empty stomach, nothing shall harm him that day until evening. Fulayh added that he thought he also said if he eats them in the evening nothing shall harm him until morning. Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz said to Amir to consider what he narrates from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he swore he neither lied about Sa'd nor did Sa'd lie about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. > **""Whoever eats seven Ajwah dates between the two lava plains of Madinah on an empty stomach, nothing shall harm him that day until evening. If he eats them in the evening, nothing shall harm him until morning.""**"
"8016","A'ishah رضي الله عنها reported from the Prophet ﷺ that whoever eats seven Ajwah dates from the dates of Aliyah in the morning, neither poison nor magic shall harm him until evening. > **""Whoever eats seven Ajwah dates from the dates of Aliyah in the morning, neither poison nor magic shall harm him until evening.""**"
"8017","Abu Khalid said he entered upon a man mixing milk with dates, who invited him near, saying the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named them the two most wholesome foods. > **""The two most wholesome foods.""**"
"8018","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه said the Messenger of Allah ﷺ distributed dates among his Companions, and some began joining two together, so he forbade joining except with the permission of one's companions."
"8019","Abu Talhah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade joining dates together."
"8020","Buraydah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said he had forbidden them from joining dates together, but since Allah has made provision ample for them, they may now join. > **""I had forbidden you from joining dates together, but Allah has now made provision ample for you, so join.""**"
"8021","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما said the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade searching through dates for what is inside them."
"8022","Abd Allah ibn Buraydah said he entered with his father upon Mu'awiyah رضي الله عنه, who seated them on the couch, brought food which they ate, then brought drink, drank, and handed to his father. Mu'awiyah then said he had been the handsomest youth of Quraysh with the finest teeth, and found nothing as delightful as in his youth except milk and a man of fine speech narrating to him."
"8023","Muslim ibn Jundub said he entered with Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما upon Ibn Muti', who greeted them with peace, mercy, welcome, and ease, and ordered a cushion. Ibn Umar said that were it not that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say three things are not refused — milk, a cushion, and oil — he would not have sat upon it. > **""Three things are not refused: milk, a cushion, and oil.""**"
"8024","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما said the Prophet ﷺ was brought cheese on a campaign and asked where it was made. They said in Persia, fearing dead meat is put in it. He told them to pierce it with the knife, mention Allah's name, and eat. > **""Pierce it with the knife, mention Allah's name, and eat.""**"
"8025","In another narration, cheese was brought and his Companions began striking it with sticks."
"8026","Maymunah, wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said the Prophet ﷺ was asked about cheese and replied to cut with the knife, mention Allah's name, and eat. > **""Cut with the knife, mention Allah's name, and eat.""**"
"8027","Ali ibn Abdillah al-Bariqi said a woman in Makkah asked him for a ruling, so he directed her to Abd Allah ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما and followed to hear. She asked about cheese made from milk with rennet, and Abd Allah replied to eat what Muslims and the People of the Book make and avoid what they do not make. She asked about locusts, and he said it is all slaughtered. She asked about gold, and he said it is disliked for men."
"8028","Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud رضي الله عنه said not to eat of cheese except what Muslims and the People of the Book make."
"8029","Al-Hasan ibn Ali رضي الله عنهما was asked about cheese and said to put the knife, mention the name, and eat."
"8030","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to take the tree as condiment, meaning olive oil, and whoever is offered perfume should take some of it. > **""Take the tree as condiment, and whoever is offered perfume should take some of it.""**"
"8031","Anas رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said how excellent a condiment is vinegar. > **""How excellent a condiment is vinegar.""**"
"8032","Al-Sa'ib ibn Yazid رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said how excellent a condiment is vinegar. > **""How excellent a condiment is vinegar.""**"
"8033","Bishr ibn Abdillah al-Khath'ami said he entered upon Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn while his son was with him, and was invited to lunch but declined as already fed. Told it was chicory, he asked what it is, and was told through his father from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said no leaf of chicory exists except upon it a drop of the water of Paradise. > **""No leaf of chicory exists except upon it a drop of the water of Paradise.""**"
"8034","Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to keep to pumpkin for it increases the brain, and to keep to lentils for they were sanctified upon the tongues of seventy Prophets. > **""Keep to pumpkin, for it increases the brain, and keep to lentils, for they were sanctified upon the tongues of seventy Prophets.""**"
"8035","Mu'adh ibn Jabal رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said if his community knew what is in fenugreek they would buy it even for its weight in gold. > **""If my community knew what is in fenugreek, they would buy it even for its weight in gold.""**"
"8036","Amr ibn Hurayth reported from his father from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that truffles are of the manna and their water is healing for the eye. > **""Truffles are of the manna, and their water is healing for the eye.""**"
"8037","Sa'id ibn Zayd رضي الله عنه reported from the Prophet ﷺ that truffles are of the manna and their water is healing for the eye. > **""Truffles are of the manna, and their water is healing for the eye.""**"
"8038","Anas رضي الله عنه said al-Ukaydir gifted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a jar of manna. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished prayer he passed the people giving each man a piece, gave Jabir a piece, then returned and gave him another. When Jabir said he had already been given once, he replied this is for the daughters of Abd Allah. > **""This is for the daughters of Abd Allah.""**"
"8039","Abu Sa'id al-Khudri رضي الله عنه said the king of Rome gifted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gifts, among them a jar of ginger. He fed each person a piece and fed Abu Sa'id a piece."
"8040","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما used to take a seed of pomegranate and eat it. Asked why, he said it reached him that no pomegranate on earth is pollinated except with a seed of Paradise, so perhaps this is it."
"8041","Rabi'ah bint Iyad al-Kilabiyyah said she heard Ali رضي الله عنه say to eat pomegranate with its fat, for it tans the stomach."
"8042","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما said Jabir ibn Abdillah came to the Prophet ﷺ with a quince brought from Ta'if and handed it to him. The Prophet ﷺ said it removes heaviness of the chest and polishes the heart. > **""It removes heaviness of the chest and polishes the heart.""**"
"8043","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said when one enters upon his Muslim brother and he feeds him, let him eat of his food without asking about it, and when he gives him drink, let him drink without asking about it. > **""When one of you enters upon his Muslim brother and he feeds him food, let him eat of his food without asking about it; and when he gives him drink, let him drink of his drink without asking about it.""**"
"8044","Salman رضي الله عنه reported from the Prophet ﷺ that whoever eats clay, it is as if he helped in killing himself. > **""Whoever eats clay, it is as if he helped in killing himself.""**"
"8045","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said Sodom and the villages around it were not destroyed until they used tooth-sticks and chewed gum in gatherings. > **""Sodom and the villages around it were not destroyed until they used tooth-sticks and chewed gum in gatherings.""**"
"8046","Abd al-Rahman ibn A'idh said Abu al-Darda رضي الله عنه was asked about leeks and onions and replied he would not eat onions after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade them."
"8047","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما said he heard the Prophet ﷺ say every pregnant slave woman is unlawful to her master until she delivers, the meat of every working donkey is unlawful, and garlic is unlawful. Then the Prophet ﷺ permitted garlic but commanded whoever eats it not to leave for the mosque until its smell departs, for it is a harm, so whoever eats it should not approach the mosque. > **""Garlic is unlawful. Garlic is permitted, but whoever eats it should not go out to the mosque until its smell departs; it is a harm, so whoever eats it should not approach the mosque.""**"
"8048","Ali رضي الله عنه said the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded them to eat garlic, saying that were it not that the angel descends upon him, he would have eaten it. > **""Eat garlic. Were it not that the angel descends upon me, I would have eaten it.""**"
"8049","Muhammad ibn Sirin said garlic would be crushed for Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما, threaded on a string, lowered into broth on a string, drawn out on a string, discarded, and the broth eaten."
"8050","Al-Zubayr رضي الله عنه reported that they slaughtered a horse in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and ate it."
"8051","Asma bint Abi Bakr رضي الله عنها said they slaughtered a horse and ate it, they and the household of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."
"8052","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما said the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the meat of domestic donkeys and commanded the meat of horses to be eaten."
"8053","Jabir ibn Abdillah رضي الله عنهما said on the day of Khaybar famine struck, people seized domestic donkeys, slaughtered them, and boiled pots. When that reached the Prophet ﷺ, he commanded them and they overturned the pots. He said Allah would bring them provision more lawful and better than this. They overturned the boiling pots that day. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the meat of tame donkeys, the meat of horses and mules, every fanged beast, every clawed bird, and forbade the tied animal, plunder, and pillage. > **""Allah shall bring you provision more lawful for you than this and better.""**"
"8054","Umm Nasr al-Muharibiyyah said a man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the meat of domestic donkeys. He asked whether it does not graze pasture and eat trees. The man said yes, so he told him to eat of its meat. > **""Does it not graze pasture and eat trees? Then eat of its meat.""**"
"8055","Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud رضي الله عنه said the Prophet ﷺ forbade the meat of domestic donkeys only because they were mounts."
"8056","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما said the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade them out of sparing the backs of the animals."
"8057","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما said the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not forbid the meat of domestic donkeys."
"8058","Abu al-Waddak said Abu Sa'id رضي الله عنه told him they took captives on the day of Khaybar and practiced withdrawal seeking ransom from their families. Some said to ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was among them, so they mentioned it to him. He replied that not from all water is the child, and when Allah decrees a matter it comes to be. They passed boiling pots, and he asked what meat this was. They said donkey meat, domestic. He told them to overturn them, so they overturned them while hungry and desiring it. They were also commanded to tie the mouths of waterskins. > **""Not from all water is the child; when Allah decrees a matter, it comes to be. What meat is this? Is it domestic or wild? Overturn them.""**"
"8059","Abu Sa'id رضي الله عنه said they campaigned with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Fadak and Khaybar, and Allah opened Fadak and Khaybar for His Messenger. People fell upon greens, garlic and onions, then returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who found their smell and was troubled, then the people returned, and he said not to eat it, and whoever eats any of it should not approach their gathering. He added that on the day of Khaybar people fell upon domestic donkeys, set up pots, and he set up his pot among them. When that reached the Prophet ﷺ he twice said he forbids it, so the pots were overturned and he overturned his pot among them. > **""Do not eat it. Whoever eats any of it should not approach our gathering. I forbid you it. I forbid you it.""**"
"8060","Abu Salit, a veteran of Badr رضي الله عنه, said the prohibition of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning the meat of donkeys reached them while at Khaybar, so they overturned them though hungry."
"8061","Abu Salit رضي الله عنه said people suffered severe hunger in the campaign of Khaybar, so they slaughtered their donkeys in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, threw them into pots, and while they boiled the prohibition descended upon the Prophet ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ announced that the prohibition of the donkeys they were cooking had descended, so the pots were overturned upon their faces. > **""The prohibition of the donkeys you are cooking has descended.""**"
"8062","Abd Allah ibn Abi Salit said the prohibition of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning eating tame donkeys reached them while the pots boiled with them, so they overturned them upon their faces."
"8063","Sinan ibn Salamah reported from his father that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded the pots to be poured out on the day of Khaybar, and they contained the meat of the people's donkeys."
"8064","Samurah ibn Jundub رضي الله عنه reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade them the domestic donkey and commanded them to throw away what they had of it, so they threw it away."
"8065","Abu Layla رضي الله عنه said they were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a campaign when the pots boiled with the meat of domestic donkeys. He ordered them poured out and distributed a sheep for every ten among them."
"8066","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما said the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seized tame donkeys on the day of Khaybar and cooked their meat. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered the pots to be overturned and forbade its meat that day."
"8067","Tha'labah ibn al-Hakam رضي الله عنه said the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ captured him when he was young, and he heard him ﷺ forbid plunder and command the pots of domestic donkey meat to be overturned."
"8068","Ka'b ibn Malik رضي الله عنه said the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade temporary marriage and the meat of domestic donkeys."
"8069","Ma'qil ibn Yasar رضي الله عنه reported that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ opened Khaybar, people seized donkeys and plundered them until the pots boiled. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was approached and told the people's donkeys had been slaughtered, so he forbade the meat of domestic donkeys, and each man overturned his vessel with the stave of his bow and the pole of his tent."
"8070","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه said the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the dung-eating animal, drinking its milk, eating it, and riding it. > **""Do not eat the dung-eating animal, do not drink its milk, and do not ride it.""**"
"8071","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reported that the Prophet ﷺ forbade on the day of the conquest of Makkah the meat of dung-eating animals, their milk, and their backs. > **""Do not eat the meat of dung-eating animals, nor their milk, nor ride their backs.""**"
"8072","Umm Nasr al-Muharibiyyah said the Prophet ﷺ was asked about the dung-eating animal. He asked whether it does not graze pasture and eat trees. Perhaps they said yes. He said then eat of its meat. > **""Does it not graze pasture and eat trees? Then eat of its meat.""**"
"8073","Jabir رضي الله عنه reported that a cow rolled onto wine and drank, so they feared for it and came to the Prophet ﷺ. He said to eat and there is no harm in eating it. > **""Eat, and there is no harm in eating it.""**"
"8074","Abu Waqid رضي الله عنه said he sat with the Prophet ﷺ when a man asked what of carrion is lawful for them in a land struck by hunger. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied that if they have neither morning drink nor evening drink and gather no greens, then they may take to it. > **""If you have neither morning drink nor evening drink, and gather no greens, then you may take to it.""**"
